TestPlan.txt - Lab 5 (ProfilePage)
Student: Leticia Benadjaoud
Project: lab02_login (branch Week5)

Setup
- Run the app (Chrome or an Android emulator / real phone).
- The correct password is ASDF.


TEST 1 - Wrong password
Steps:
1. Type any login name.
2. Type a wrong password (example: 1234).
3. Click the Login button.
Expected result:
- The stop sign image is shown.
- The app stays on the first page (no navigation, no Snackbar).

TEST 2 - Correct password and navigation
Steps:
1. Type the login name "Leticia".
2. Type the password ASDF.
3. Click the Login button.
4. In the Save Login Info dialog, click Yes.
Expected result:
- The light bulb image is shown.
- The app navigates to the ProfilePage.
- A Snackbar shows "Welcome Back Leticia" (the login name from the first page).

TEST 3 - ProfilePage layout
Steps:
1. Look at the ProfilePage after Test 2.
Expected result:
- Four TextFields: First Name, Last Name, Phone Number, Email address.
- Phone Number has two buttons beside it (telephone and SMS).
- Email address has one button beside it (mail).
- No layout error (TextFields are inside Flexible).


TEST 4 - Telephone button
Steps:
1. Type a phone number (example: 6135551234).
2. Click the telephone button.
Expected result:
- The phone dialer opens with that number ("tel:" protocol).
- If the field is empty, nothing happens.
(Note: on a computer browser this cannot open, so test on an emulator or phone.)


TEST 5 - SMS button
Steps:
1. Type a phone number.
2. Click the SMS button.
Expected result:
- The text messaging application opens for that number ("sms:" protocol).


TEST 6 - Email button
Steps:
1. Type an email address (example: test@example.com).
2. Click the mail button.
Expected result:
- The email program opens with a new email addressed to that address
  ("mailto:" protocol).


TEST 7 - Data is saved and loaded (repository)
Steps:
1. On the ProfilePage, type a first name, last name, phone number and email.
2. Close the app completely.
3. Run the app again, log in with ASDF and click Yes in the dialog.
Expected result:
- The four TextFields are already filled with the values typed before.
- The data was saved by saveData() when the text changed (addListener)
  and loaded by loadData() when the app started.

TEST 8 - Translation on the first page and ProfilePage
- All texts switch to English, and back to French when clicked again.